<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Oswald:wght@200..700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">

<style>
    body {
        font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', 'Roboto', sans-serif;
        background-image: url(<%= image_path('backgroundaboutus.jpg') %>);
        background-position: center;
        background-attachment: fixed;
    }

    .faq-hero {
        text-align: center;
        margin: 3rem auto 2rem;
        padding: 0 1.5rem;
    }

    .faq-title {
        font-family: 'Oswald', sans-serif;
        color: #a0c9ff;
        font-size: 2.5rem;
        margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    }

    .faq-subtitle {
        color: #cecdcd;
        font-size: 1.1rem;
        margin: 0 auto;
        max-width: 720px;
    }

    .faq-container {
        max-width: 980px;
        margin: 0 auto 4rem;
        padding: 0 1.5rem;
        display: grid;
        gap: 1rem;
    }

    .faq-card {
        background: #ffffff;
        border-radius: 10px;
        box-shadow: 0 2px 12px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08);
        border-left: 4px solid #044caa;
        overflow: hidden;
        transition: transform 0.2s, box-shadow 0.2s;
    }

    .faq-card:hover {
        transform: translateY(-2px);
        box-shadow: 0 4px 16px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.12);
    }

    .faq-question {
        list-style: none;
        cursor: pointer;
        padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
        font-weight: 700;
        color: #044caa;
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: space-between;
        gap: 1rem;
    }

    .faq-question::-webkit-details-marker {
        display: none;
    }

    .faq-question .indicator {
        width: 26px;
        height: 26px;
        border-radius: 50%;
        background: #e8fff1;
        color: #044caa;
        display: inline-flex;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: center;
        font-size: 1.1rem;
        flex-shrink: 0;
        transition: transform 0.2s;
    }

    details[open] .faq-question .indicator {
        transform: rotate(45deg);
    }

    .faq-answer {
        padding: 0 1.5rem 1.25rem;
        color: #555;
        line-height: 1.6;
        background: #fafafa;
        border-top: 1px solid #eee;
    }



    .faq-cta {
        max-width: 980px;
        margin: 2rem auto 4rem;
        padding: 1.5rem;
        background: #ffffff;
        border-radius: 10px;
        box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08);
        border-left: 4px solid #044caa;
        text-align: center;
    }

    .faq-cta h3 {
        margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
        color: #044caa;
        font-family: 'Oswald', sans-serif;
        font-size: 1.5rem;
    }

    .faq-cta p {
        margin: 0 0 1rem;
        color: #666;
    }

    .faq-cta a {
        display: inline-block;
        padding: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
        background: #044caa;
        color: #fff;
        border-radius: 6px;
        text-decoration: none;
        font-weight: 600;
        transition: background 0.2s;
    }

    .faq-cta a:hover {
        background: #0557c2;
    }

    @media (max-width: 768px) {
        .faq-title {
            font-size: 2rem;
        }

        .faq-question {
            flex-direction: column;
            align-items: flex-start;
        }
    }
</style>

<section class="faq-hero">
    <h1 class="faq-title">Frequently Asked Questions</h1>
    <p class="faq-subtitle">Quick answers to common questions about Pseudocoder, how compilations work, and how to get the most out of your sessions.</p>
</section>

<section class="faq-container">
    <details class="faq-card" open>
        <summary class="faq-question">
            What is Pseudocoder?
            <span class="indicator">+</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
            Pseudocoder is a lightweight, browser-based program for translating ideas into structured pseudocode and previewing compilation results. It is designed to keep you focused on logic first, then language specifics.

        </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-card">
        <summary class="faq-question">
            Which languages are supported?
            <span class="indicator">+</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
            You can compile or translate into the core languages shown in our services. The list updates as new languages are added, so check our services page for the latest updates.
        </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-card">
        <summary class="faq-question">
            Do I need an account to use it?
            <span class="indicator">+</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
            You can start immediately as a guest. Creating an account lets you save compilations, revisit history, and sync sessions across devices.
        </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-card">
        <summary class="faq-question">
            Where do my compilations go?
            <span class="indicator">+</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
            Saved compilations appear in your history panel and are tied to your account. Guest sessions cannot save their compilations and will have to save it manually before recompiling.
        </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-card">
        <summary class="faq-question">
            Can I upload a file instead of pasting code?
            <span class="indicator">+</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
            Yes. Use the file input in the compile form to upload a text file. The file name is shown in the editor so you can review before compiling.
        </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-card">
        <summary class="faq-question">
            How secure is my data?
            <span class="indicator">+</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
            Your data is stored only to provide the requested experience. Avoid sharing sensitive information in your projects, and sign out on shared devices for extra safety.
        </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-card">
        <summary class="faq-question">
            Why is a compilation failing?
            <span class="indicator">+</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
            A failure usually means there is a syntax or formatting issue in the input. Try simplifying your pseudocode, then recompile in small steps to isolate the issue.
        </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-card">
        <summary class="faq-question">
            Can I suggest a feature?
            <span class="indicator">+</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
            Absolutely. Use the contact page to send ideas, or reach out with feedback on the latest release. We prioritize features that improve clarity and learning.
        </div>
    </details>
    <details class="faq-card">
        <summary class="faq-question">
            Is Miguel single?
            <span class="indicator">+</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
            Yes, he is single and ready to mingle. Feel free to message him at 917-452-9483, he is waiting.
        </div>
    </details>
</section>

<section class="faq-cta">
    <h3>Still have questions?</h3>
    <p>Send a message and we will get back to you with a clear answer.</p>
    <a href="/contactus">Contact the team</a>
</section>